To: Knight, Anita <Anita.Knight@Justice.gov.uk>
Cc: Alexis Campbell KC <ACampbellKC@29br.co.uk>; Brent Molyneux KC <BMolyne=
ux@29br.co.uk>
Subject: BV20D01752 Zahmoul vs Zahmoul - FW: Material Event - SPAC merger e=
ffective date 8 February 2024 -Nasdaq ticker BRLS
Importance: High

=20

Dear Anita,

=20

I hope you are well.

I would be most grateful if you could please pass this on to His Lordship.=20

This is material to the case and to the Final Hearing which took place befo=
re His Lordship on 19th - 28th February 2024.=20

I am copying counsels on both sides.

Thank you very much.

=20

With my kind wishes,

Nadia

=20

=20

Your Lordship,

=20

I am sincerely sorry to trouble Your Lordship so soon after the Final Heari=
ng. The matter of Oxus Acquisition Corp. is very material to the case and ca=
me to my attention almost immediately after the trial ended.  Despite writin=
g to the respondent one week ago to request an explanation, we have not rece=
ived a reply.=20

=20

This open-ended situation is very harmful to me. I feel powerless, vulnerab=
le, and extremely distressed. I find it impossible to put the children=E2=80=99s a=
nd my future into the respondent=E2=80=99s hands and wait without knowing how long=
 I must wait.

=20

I put the matter into Your Lordship=E2=80=99s hands and if one week is not enough=
, I am happy to wait as long as Your Lordship would like me to.=20

=20

At the Final Hearing and under oath, the respondent represented that his sh=
ares in Oxus Acquisition Corp. were =E2=80=9Cworth zero=E2=80=9D. In the asset schedule =
submitted for the Final Hearing, he reported 50,000 shares at a value of $0.=
00.=20

=20

This is factually incorrect and constitutes a false statement.

=20
The respondent was appointed to the Board of Directors of Oxus Acquisition =
Corp. on 1st June 2022 and=20
On 7th June 2022 Form 3 =E2=80=9CInitial Statement of Beneficial Ownership of Sec=
urities=E2=80=9D was filed with the SEC.
PAGE 340 of SEC PROSPECTUS (attached): =E2=80=9COn June 7, 2022, 50,000 Founder S=
hares were transferred to Mr. Karim Zahmoul by the Sponsor. The fair value o=
f the 50,000 Founder Shares granted to the Mr. Karim Zahmoul on June 7, 2022=
, was $0.02 million or $0.33 per share. The Founder Shares were granted subj=
ect to a performance condition (i.e., the occurrence of a Business Combinati=
on)=E2=80=9D.
The Founder Shares were granted subject to a performance condition (i.e., t=
he occurrence of a Business Combination).
The Business Combination occurred on 7th February 2024.
Newco began trading on Nasdaq on 8th February 2024 under the ticker symbol =
BRLS.
The Founder Shares lock-up period is defined in page 43 of the Prospectus f=
iled with the SEC (attached) and in the attached SEC Filings Excerpts.
=20

Conclusion:=20

The Final Hearing started on 19th February 2024.=20

At the time of the Final Hearing and when he testified under oath, the resp=
ondent knew (i) that the Business Combination had occurred and (ii) that the=
 value of his 50,000 Founders Shares was not zero.

=20

Email sent to the respondent=E2=80=99s solicitors on 29th February 2024 (attached=
):

=E2=80=9CDear Valeria,

We attach documents in relation to the SPAC merger between Oxus and Boreali=
s which closed on 7th February 2024. The post-merger stock has been trading =
on the NASDAQ since the 8th February 2024. In his ES2 dated 19.02.2024 he as=
cribes a nil value to his OXUS equity. Given that the merged entity (ticker =
BRLS) is trading at a stock price of $9.20 (and your client had 50,000 share=
s in the pre-merger OXUS) please can you explain the value of his stockholdi=
ng with reference to the attached documents and any others in your clients p=
ossession =E2=80=93 and why he ascribed a nil value to his equity in the ES2.=20

We look forward to hearing from you.=E2=80=9D

=20

Respectfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

=20

On 29/02/2024, 3:41=E2=80=AFPM, "Nadia" <nadia@rosekross.com> wrote:

=20

Dear Brent,

=20

THE FOLLOWING SHOWS THAT ONCE AGAIN, THE RESPONDENT IS TAKING ME AND THE CO=
URT FOR FOOLS. Please send to the judge

=20

The Oxus and Borealis M&A closed on 7 February 2024 and the Newco began tra=
ding on Nasdaq on 8 February 2024 under the ticker symbol BRSL.

=20
The attached forms from the SEC provide documentary evidence of the followi=
ng facts:
=20
The respondent has 50,000 Founder shares
The grant value is $0.33 per share
The shares are now listed on Nasdaq under ticker symbol BRLS
The current market price is $9.20
The current price appreciation (book value): 2588%
The current market value of the respondent=E2=80=99s shares: $443,500
Lock-up period: one year=20
=20
Warrants and Options granted to directors and founders have not been disclo=
sed.
=20

=20
The Final Hearing before Justice MacDonald started on Monday 19th February.=
 During his testimonies under oath the respondent represented that his share=
s in Oxus Acquisition Fund were worth zero. He also instructed his counsel t=
o represent to the Court that his =E2=80=9Cshares in Oxus were on the side and wer=
e worth zero=E2=80=9D. This is a false representation. The shares owned by the res=
pondent are worth $443,500. The lock-up period does not define the value of =
the shares. The respondent can borrow against the shares during the lock-up =
and can monetize them. He knows this. The key metric which determines the va=
lue of the shares is the CLOSING OF THE MERGER TRANSACTION. This happened on=
 7 February 2024, 11 days before the trial started.=20
THAT IS THE DATE WHICH DETERMINES THE VALUE OF THE RESPONDENT=E2=80=99S SHARES.

=20

=20

With kind wishes,

Nadia

